It is given, $\cot A, \cot B$ and $\cot C$ are in AP .
$\begin{array}{ll}\Rightarrow & 2 \cot B=\cot A+\cot C \\ \Rightarrow & 2 \frac{\cos B}{\sin B}=\frac{\cos A}{\sin A}+\frac{\cos C}{\sin C} \\ \because & \frac{\sin A}{a}=\frac{\sin B}{b}=\frac{\sin C}{c}=k \\ \Rightarrow & \frac{2 \cos B}{k b}=\frac{\cos A}{a k}+\frac{\cos C}{c k} \\ \Rightarrow & \frac{2 \cos B}{b}=\frac{\cos A}{a}+\frac{\cos C}{c}\end{array} \begin{aligned}$& \Rightarrow \quad $\frac{2}{b} \left[\frac{a^2+c^2-b^2}{2 a c}\right]=\frac{1}{a}\left[\frac{b^2+c^2-a^2}{2 b c}\right]\\ &+\frac{1}{c}\left[\frac{a^2+b^2-c^2}{2 a b}\right]\end{aligned}\begin{aligned}& \Rightarrow \quad \frac{2\left(a^2+c^2-b^2\right)}{2 a b c}=\frac{1}{2 a b c}\\ & {\left[\left(b^2+c^2-a^2\right)+\left(a^2+b^2-c^2\right)\right] }\end{aligned}\begin{array}{rlrl}\Rightarrow & & 2\left(a^2+c^2-b^2\right) & =2 b^2 \\ \Rightarrow & a^2+c^2 & =2 b^2\end{array}
$\therefore a², b²$ and $c^2$ are in AP.$
